Title: Detect attachment language and apply D6 per language
Created: 2026-09-02
Author: codex
Blocked-by: 0554

--- log ---
2026-09-02T15:23Z codex created

--- body ---
## Context

The 2026-09-02 rendering ruling amends D6 to first-with-text per detected
language. Twin attachments in different languages are both body-text sources;
same-language siblings retain D6's deterministic first choice and stored skip
reason. This ticket owns the derived attachment-language field and the choice
function. It never writes a language or relation into Zotero.

## Actions

1. Add a small license-clean language detector on extracted attachment text.
2. Store its normalized language identifier as derived per-attachment state and
   include detector identity in the derivation key.
3. Change D6's choice function to select the first attachment per language by
   ascending `dateAdded`, key tie-break.
4. Report same-language skips and per-language coverage through the existing
   ledger/status path.

## Test

- A bilingual item indexes one EN and one VI attachment.
- Two same-language attachments index only the deterministic first and record
  the other one's reason.
- A detector-version or language-result change re-derives the choice.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Attachment language is derived, keyed and stored without altering Zotero.
- [ ] D6 selects one body attachment per detected language.
- [ ] The bilingual and same-language controls pass.
- [ ] `make check` and `./tickets/erg check` pass.
